Recommends: vulkan-validationlayers
Suggests: desktopvideo
Description: Live video switcher for Linux and NVIDIA, up to 8K 59.94p
 8Kloud Switcher takes OMT, SDI (Blackmagic DeckLink) and SRT sources, mixes
 them on the GPU through Vulkan compute, and sends program out over OMT, SDI
 and SRT (HEVC or AV1 via NVENC) while recording HEVC/AAC Matroska locally.
 .
 It carries a full audio mixer with per-input frame sync, two alpha downstream
 keyers, paced local clip playlists, still-image inputs, a clean feed without
 DSK graphics, a browser-based production console served by the switcher
 itself, and the multiview wall as an OMT source. A plain-text TCP control
 port drives it remotely, with a Bitfocus Companion module supplied.
 .
 This package ships the console (8kloud-switcher: engine + web GUI), the
 headless engine (kloud-headless) and the bench tools (kloud-testgen,
 kloud-latmeter).
 It requires an NVIDIA GPU with a current proprietary driver.
